WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.960
Nowhere is more secure than an SCP Foundation
facility.

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:09.530
They make Fort Knox look like a revolving
door with a spare key under the mat.

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:15.249
That’s why when someone or something can
infiltrate without even being noticed it’s

00:00:15.249 --> 00:00:17.320
considered a major threat.

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:22.630
And doing exactly that is what put a mysterious
group of insurgents known as The Serpent’s

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:24.470
Hand on the map.

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:29.849
But this Group of Interest isn’t just infamous
for its ability to sneak into Foundation strongholds.

00:00:29.849 --> 00:00:34.320
Like a lot of the SCP Foundation’s biggest
threats, from the Scarlet King to the Chaos

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:39.180
Insurgency, the roots of the Serpent’s Hand
are closer than they think.

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:43.020
The Foundation’s first official brush with
the Serpent’s Hand came shortly after they

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:50.020
contained SCP-268: an Irish tweed-wool newsboy
cap believed to have been created some time

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:51.820
in the 1800s.

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:55.980
The only identifying mark on the cap is a
label with the following phrase written in

00:00:55.980 --> 00:01:01.760
Middle Irish: “The Garden is the Serpent's
Place” - initially believed to be a reference

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:04.620
to the serpent in the biblical Garden of Eden.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:10.540
This Euclid-Class SCP is a double-edged sword:
It gives the user a useful supernatural ability

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:14.420
at a terrifying supernatural cost.

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:19.370
Anyone wearing the cap appears so utterly
unremarkable that nobody is able to take notice

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:23.970
of them, and when they leave a person’s
general area of awareness, they’re quickly

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:24.970
forgotten.

00:01:24.970 --> 00:01:27.829
The user isn’t invisible, but they might
as well be.

00:01:27.829 --> 00:01:32.630
If you’re a person whose line of work involves
sneaking and subterfuge, or you’re just

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:36.380
a major introvert, this sounds like a dream
come true.

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:42.409
However, like a lot of anomalies, this dream
can quickly become a nightmare.

00:01:42.409 --> 00:01:47.549
If someone wears the cap repeatedly, or for
too long at one time, they risk the effects

00:01:47.549 --> 00:01:51.369
of the cap becoming permanent, even when it’s
removed.

00:01:51.369 --> 00:01:57.659
You can become a forgotten person, impossible
to notice and remember, even to those closest

00:01:57.659 --> 00:01:58.659
to you.

00:01:58.659 --> 00:02:03.780
Why anyone would want such a fate is a mystery,
so it came as a surprise to the Foundation

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:09.130
when the hat suddenly disappeared from secure
containment, replaced by a note reading, “Thanks,

00:02:09.130 --> 00:02:11.220
I needed my hat back.

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:12.220
~ L.S."

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:14.580
Who was this mysterious L.S.?

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:18.390
And was the anomaly truly theirs prior to
containment?

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:23.510
Scientists, security officials, and administrators
hoped this would be an isolated incident,

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:26.080
but L.S. was far from done.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:30.800
And even worse for the Foundation, L.S. was
now armed with a perfect anomalous tool to

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:33.880
make their next containment breach even smoother.

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:39.550
The next incident was known as Security Breach
Incident X23, and was committed against the

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:44.850
extremely valuable Site 19 - the largest Foundation
Site there is.

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:49.590
Most humiliating of all for the Foundation
security team working there, security footage

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:54.040
indicated that L.S. simply strolled into the
base without being noticed.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:57.270
SCP-268 was working wonders.

00:02:57.270 --> 00:03:04.570
This time, L.S. had a new target: SCP-914,
an anomalous machine also known as The Clockworks.

00:03:04.570 --> 00:03:10.550
This machine, originally tested by the famously
emotionless Dr. Charles Gears, has the ability

00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:15.920
to “refine” any object placed into its
chambers into a greater version of their original

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:20.310
selves - often with strange and anomalous
results.

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:24.570
You can probably see why someone wanting to
utilize anomalies for their own gain would

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:27.360
take such a keen interest in this one.

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:33.880
L.S. breezed past the guards, inexplicably
destroyed the file for SCP-407 - a taped song

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:38.980
that causes unchecked cellular growth - and
made their way towards 914.

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:45.120
Unfortunately, a researcher who was working
on 914 was murdered by L.S. during the breach.

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:48.290
We have no idea what they did with 914.

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:53.530
Perhaps they refined 268 to act as an even
more effective stealth tool, without its unpleasant

00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:54.820
side effects.

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:57.870
Maybe they made the daring move of refining
themself.

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:59.480
We’ll never know.

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:03.690
All we do know is that this time, L.S. left
a letter.

00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:08.650
It was long, rambling, and philosophical,
with no incriminating information that could

00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:11.610
be used to identify the mysterious figure.

00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:13.310
They signed off the letter with:

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:19.790
“I leave you with one final truth; The Garden
is the Serpent's place; the divinities of

00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:25.540
fear and order who come to walk in the cool
evening air are only visitors.

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:30.760
Do not fail to see the evil hiding in the
light, nor the aromatic beauty of the palest

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:32.820
flower of darkness.

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:35.320
Signed Sincerely,
L.S.”

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:39.760
These repeated references to the “Serpent”
clued the Foundation in on the affiliation

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:45.420
of this new troublemaker: A growing Group
of Interest named The Serpent’s Hand.

00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:48.620
But really, who are The Serpent’s Hand?

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:49.900
What do they want?

00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:54.530
What is their connection to other active groups
of interest, like the Chaos Insurgency and

00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:56.250
the Global Occult Coalition?

00:04:56.250 --> 00:05:02.160
And was this mysterious L.S. figure the leader
of the group, or just another agent?

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:06.360
These were all questions on the minds of the
Foundation’s best and brightest tactical

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:09.850
thinkers, but the answers didn’t come easy.

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:14.680
During the Serpent’s Hand investigations,
the Foundation found an unlikely ally in what

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:19.150
is usually one of their biggest opponents:
The Global Occult Coalition.

00:05:19.150 --> 00:05:24.080
The GOC had dealt with the Serpent’s Hand
before, and understood their central philosophy.

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:28.760
Whereas the Foundation and the GOC were both
committed to acting in secret and maintaining

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:33.980
a sense of normality, the Serpent’s Hand
wanted the exact opposite: They wanted to

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:39.340
destroy the secrecy around the anomalous and
supernatural, and reveal the existence of

00:05:39.340 --> 00:05:41.170
it all to the general public.

00:05:41.170 --> 00:05:46.210
While the Foundation and the GOC think this
is crazy, the Serpent’s Hand aren’t just

00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:49.520
insane anarchists who want to unleash chaos
across the world.

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:53.810
In fact, they actually have some pretty interesting
points.

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:57.920
The Serpent’s Hand acknowledges that the
supernatural can be dangerous, but much like

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:02.870
natural disasters and crime, will the public
benefit from not knowing about them?

00:06:02.870 --> 00:06:07.670
Members of the Serpent’s Hand also fight
for the rights of non-violent anomalous entities,

00:06:07.670 --> 00:06:10.880
particularly sentient and sapient beings.

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:15.060
They find the Foundation’s habit of containing
them and the GOC’s habit of killing them

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:21.240
barbaric, and will openly use and collaborate
with anomalies to further their goals - like

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:26.280
how L.S. is a keen operator of 268 for their
infiltration missions.

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:31.690
At least one hundred and seventy-seven individuals
belonging to the Serpent's Hand have been

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:36.730
identified, many of which have actively performed
raids on Foundation sites across the globe.

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:40.870
It was a mystery to the Foundation how such
a small number of members could run rings

00:06:40.870 --> 00:06:46.410
around them, and seemingly be everywhere at
once, until a revelation was delivered by

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:48.530
the Global Occult Coalition.

00:06:48.530 --> 00:06:53.980
The Serpent’s Hand have an informal headquarters
in an anomalous location known as The Wanderer’s

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:59.010
Library - an ancient and seemingly limitless
archive containing every book from every dimension

00:06:59.010 --> 00:07:00.440
in the multiverse.

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:05.350
This location exists outside of space and
time, and can be accessed through a global

00:07:05.350 --> 00:07:09.410
network of inter-dimensional portals known
as The Ways.

00:07:09.410 --> 00:07:14.120
Like a supernatural guerilla soldier, members
of the Serpent’s Hand would exit from one

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:19.840
of The Ways, raid a Foundation or GOC Site,
and then escape back into another one of The

00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:23.610
Ways, using the Wanderer’s Library as a
safe zone.

00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:29.350
The library was a convenient way to access
and steal from sites worldwide with impunity,

00:07:29.350 --> 00:07:33.240
increasing their stock of anomalous items
and beings each time.

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:38.180
While performing raids and stealing anomalies
feels like textbook Chaos Insurgency behavior,

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:43.960
the Serpent’s Hand have an extremely frosty
relationship with the Insurgency, too - often

00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:47.770
seeing them as greedy, erratic, and short
sighted.

00:07:47.770 --> 00:07:52.460
The Serpent’s Hand has a series of catchy
nicknames for its various foes - it refers

00:07:52.460 --> 00:07:57.050
to the Foundation as “The Jailers”, the
GOC as “The Book Burners”, and the Chaos

00:07:57.050 --> 00:07:59.620
Insurgency as “The Mad Men.”

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:05.480
The Foundation even formed a new task force,
known as The Bookworms, explicitly for Serpent’s

00:08:05.480 --> 00:08:06.840
Hand related missions.

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:11.330
While the Foundation has engaged in a number
of raids and skirmishes on the Serpent’s

00:08:11.330 --> 00:08:15.900
Hand since their feud began, they’ve never
been able to gather any information about

00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:17.800
who gives the orders.

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:22.160
Only the Global Occult Coalition have been
able to successfully perform a raid on the

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:26.710
Wanderer’s Library, an act that was extremely
difficult and costly.

00:08:26.710 --> 00:08:32.140
It also earned the GOC a spot as the Serpent’s
Hand’s public enemy number one, a role the

00:08:32.140 --> 00:08:34.919
Foundation isn’t eager to take from them.

00:08:34.919 --> 00:08:38.969
With the unlimited knowledge present in the
Wanderer’s Library, and the mysterious nature

00:08:38.969 --> 00:08:43.770
of their command structure, this group manages
to be a formidable enemy for the Foundation

00:08:43.770 --> 00:08:45.700
despite its small size.

00:08:45.700 --> 00:08:50.050
What the Foundation doesn’t know is that
there actually is no command structure for

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:51.210
the Serpent’s Hand.

00:08:51.210 --> 00:08:55.750
They’re a decentralized group of splinter
cells and lone wolves acting out a philosophy

00:08:55.750 --> 00:08:58.270
rather than a specific mission.

00:08:58.270 --> 00:09:03.290
This way of working is so alien to the highly
regimented structures of the Foundation and

00:09:03.290 --> 00:09:07.160
the GOC, it’s no surprise that they’re
stumped by it.

00:09:07.160 --> 00:09:12.250
This still leaves us with one more question
central to the whole mystery: If not the leader

00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:16.950
of this organization, who exactly is L.S?

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:22.700
To answer this, we must return once more to
Dr. Charles Ogden Gears - the cold and robotic

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:27.440
Foundation scientist in charge of SCP-914
research.

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:31.420
If all the ways Dr. Gears has been described
so far has made you think he wouldn’t be

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:36.070
a particularly warm and loving father, you’d
be absolutely right.

00:09:36.070 --> 00:09:39.260
Just ask his estranged daughter, Alison Chao.

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:44.070
Alison never forgave Gears for abandoning
her and her mother, and she now does everything

00:09:44.070 --> 00:09:48.600
she can to get revenge on him and his precious
Foundation.

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:52.970
But here’s the problem: The Gears of this
dimension is not the only one who has a child

00:09:52.970 --> 00:09:54.430
with an axe to grind.

00:09:54.430 --> 00:09:59.950
Gears has been a deadbeat dad in a number
of dimensions, so much so that these disgruntled

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:06.200
daughters converge in the Wanderer’s Library
to plot their revenge across dimensions together.

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:11.589
This collective of Alison Chao’s, sometimes
believed to be just one Alison, is known to

00:10:11.589 --> 00:10:14.240
the Foundation as the Black Queen.

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:19.270
However, they themselves more commonly refer
to their daughter support group turned terrorist

00:10:19.270 --> 00:10:22.010
organization as the “Little Sisters.”

00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:27.290
Or, if you’d prefer, the abbreviation “L.S.”

00:10:27.290 --> 00:10:31.920
While the Serpent’s Hand has no leader,
the Little Sisters are some of its most devoted

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:34.029
and dangerous warriors.

00:10:34.029 --> 00:10:40.010
They’re intelligent, coordinated, and - due
to their obsession with Dr. Gears - personally

00:10:40.010 --> 00:10:43.490
invested in hitting the Foundation where it
hurts.

00:10:43.490 --> 00:10:48.890
After all, that’s what the Serpent’s Hand
is all about: Striking out against the oppressors

00:10:48.890 --> 00:10:54.640
who keep a stranglehold on the truth, throwing
off the chains imposed by the Foundation,

00:10:54.640 --> 00:10:59.170
and the violence visited upon anomalies by
the Global Occult Coalition.

00:10:59.170 --> 00:11:04.770
If the Serpent’s Hand gets their way, one
day there may be a glorious world where humans

00:11:04.770 --> 00:11:07.390
and anomalies knowingly coexist.

00:11:07.390 --> 00:11:10.400
It’s a nice thing to imagine.

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:12.200
Utopian, even.

00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:15.990
But the Foundation’s greatest concern about
the Serpent’s Hand isn’t that they’re

00:11:15.990 --> 00:11:18.660
evil - it’s that they’re naive.

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:22.540
While the Serpent’s Hand don’t wish to
usher in the apocalypse, it doesn’t mean

00:11:22.540 --> 00:11:25.350
they won’t by complete accident.

00:11:25.350 --> 00:11:30.890
Their kindness and understanding towards anomalies
may one day make them a perfect band of useful

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:34.529
idiots for an entity with far darker intentions.

00:11:34.529 --> 00:11:40.460
And one day, they may just release something
that really would be better locked away...

00:11:40.460 --> 00:11:48.960
Now check out “SCP Chaos Insurgency Explained”
and “SCP - 001 - Which Is The Real SCP - 001”

00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:52.369
for more deep lore from the world of the SCP
Foundation!

